  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF 2014-2017 A National Strategy to Protect  the HR of Girls and Boys - UNICEF Child Protection 2014-2017</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UNICEF 2014-2017 En nationell strategi till skydd f&#xf6;r flickors och pojkars MR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UNICEF 2014-2017 Program f&#xf6;r att st&#xf6;dja utvecklingen av system p&#xe5;     national, regional och lokal niv&#xe5; till skydd f&#xf6;r flickors och pojkars m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter i Guatemala.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF 2014-2017 Programme to support the development of protection   systems on national, regional and local levels in order to protect    the human rights of girls and boys in Guatemala.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;Support to the National Strategy for Protection of the Human Rights of Children 2014-2017&quot;, extended to 2108, in the total amount of SEK 54 600 000, seeks to help child and adolescent victims of threats and violations exercise their human rights in a coordinated and decentralized child protection system. Construction of a consolidated national system will strengthen inter-institutional coordination with clear roles and responsibilities, and improve State protection services and attention to child and adolescent victims of violence. The intervention builds on results of previous, long-term cooperation between UNICEF and Sida in Guatemala, related to children&apos;s special protection needs and respect for child rights.
The intervention also seeks to identify, evidence and question social practises which promote violence and exclusion of children and adolescents, reproduced in State institutions in charge of protection of minors. The objective is not only to strengthen the relevant State institutions, but also impact positively on attitudes towards minors in need of special protection and the institutional practises when attending child victims.
Within program framework, UNICEF coordinates and works with nine different State institutions, including the National Police, the Judicial, Attorney General, Ministry for Foreign Affairs, and agencies directly in charge of child welfare and protection. It also coordinates with civil society organizations dedicated to child rights and protection.</narrative>
  </description>
